{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789425038,"nonce":"d/iwaoL5TRSa6k30+sOy1nY3YDg=","message":"Step 3 landed as the commit after 5574770, and not as an Ash change.\n\nThe plan was a trailer after every hl_type ash lays out, so word zero of a Haxe object reads as a descriptor. Two things against it once the sites were surveyed: a bound method's closure type is the `closure_type` field HashLink's `hl_type_fun` embeds (hl.h, which HDLLs link against), followed by the `closure` signature, so it can never carry a trailer and every closure would have stayed a cell; and the same result comes without touching a type at all. Every descriptor's hl_type prefix now names one static of the core's as its mark bits (heap::CORE_MARK), which no HashLink type's do, so protocol::desc_of tells a descriptor from a bare hl_type by two loads and answers the foreign descriptor Ash registers at install (set_foreign_descriptor) for the latter. A Haxe object is a core object as it is: language_of, Send::proto, describe all work on the object, it crosses as itself, and Ash's protocol entries work on the object rather than through a cell.\n\nWhat it does not change: a Haxe object still has no word to spare for a shadow, so the Wren adapter finds the cell it holds a Haxe object through by address, in the cell module's map (moved from Ash's side to Wren's). The per-crossing cost of a Haxe object entering Wren is therefore the same map lookup as before (same object Haxe→Wren 52 ns, fresh 125–145, returned 114; within noise of step 2). Dropping the map needs a word before every Haxe object, a 16-byte prefix as Wren's objects have, which is Ash's allocator and its compiled bump path: 16 bytes on every Haxe object, crossing or not. Left as the user's call.\n\nAlso: the caribou-wren heartbeat test (idle_garbage_is_collected_on_the_heartbeat) fails since wren_lift 2bf3f74 (e61b255: a compiled loop header loads from the safepoint page), with or without this change; noted on 16d8592.","files":null}]}